# AoC 2022 Day 8 Part 1 — the full visibility solve.
#
# A tree is visible when it sits on an edge or when every tree before it in
# some direction is shorter. The positional Count Cells form binds
# (grid, row, col), and the row/col builtins slice the lines of sight;
# short-circuit `or` keeps the empty-prefix max() calls unevaluated on edges.
# For the example grid the answer is 21.
Cursed Energy: input.txt
Shikigami: Digit Grid
Maximum Technique: Count Cells
    Using: (g, r, c) -> r = 0 or r = rows(g) - 1 or c = 0 or c = cols(g) - 1 or max(take(row(g, r), c)) < at(g, r, c) or max(drop(row(g, r), c + 1)) < at(g, r, c) or max(take(col(g, c), r)) < at(g, r, c) or max(drop(col(g, c), r + 1)) < at(g, r, c)
Reveal: stdout
